<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liudolf, Duke of Saxony</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/866">866</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Liudolf was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> count who led the eastern Saxons in the mid ninth century under the Carolingian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-german">Louis the German</a>. With his wife Oda he founded a convent in 852, which moved to Gandersheim in 856 and became one of the great imperial abbeys. He is regarded as the ancestor of the Liudolfing or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottonian-dynasty">Ottonian dynasty</a>, which produced the kings and emperors <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-fowler">Henry the Fowler</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-i">Otto I</a>.</p></div>
